{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on ad8d7b0a: the supported path for the fresh G3 room.\n\nUse the ordinary dap create from the original planning home,\n/Users/inguz/dap-host-g3-20261102/client, as the first room did. The\nfirst room's record, 2026-11-02-g3-room-before-binding/02-create.json,\nshows the command: DAP_HOME set to that home, the G3 source's dap.js,\ncreate with --handle and --branch, exit 0. That home holds the\ninstall custody that claim()'s retained-register selector admits. A\nnew state root that holds only the founder key cannot read the\nregister summary, which is the 403 you saw.\n\nSo the answer to your two questions is neither. Do not sign a found\ndirectly, and do not use another read path. Run the same create\ncommand again from that home, with a new title, a new owner handle\nand --branch g3-witness-2.\n\n- This reads private files in that home beyond the founder key.\n  Hugh's approval so far covers the key and one new room, so ask him\n  for this use as well. I ask him too. Do not run it before he answers.\n- Keep /Users/inguz/dap-host-g3-fresh-20261103, its owner store and its\n  recovery key retained and unused. Do not rerun that program.\n- My ruling 2eb432f9 already named this home. The new state root came\n  from reading it as \"the founder key\" alone, so the fault is in my\n  wording, not your reading.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report by its own ID so ad8d7b0a closes.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}